review when the proposal contains no significant planning, design and engineering issues.At this time,
staff does not recommend an expedited review, as a few issues remain, as outlined below.
EXECUTIVE SUMMARY: This 3 acre project proposes 2mixed-use building lots,94-plex lots, and a
single, commonly-owned lot intended to provide access, parking, and landscaping on the site.The WAPA
trans i mission lines and Greenway buffer this site from the residential neighborhood to the north,
presenting substantial physical impediments for any practical development.The mixed-use buildings
would front along Snyder. The Preliminary Plat has been submitted in conjunction with a Zone Change
request from A1 to MUR.A zone change from A1 is a prerequisite to any development as it is a County
zone district.Plan Cheyenne does not contemplate any future land uses with A1 as an underlying zone
district, and theUDC does not provide regulations for A1 as it is not designated in the development code.
In general, the proposalis consistent with Plan Cheyenne.However, design requirements related
primarily to the residential portion needs to be finalized before the Final Plat is presented.These include
on-site circulation and appropriate lot typefor the4-plexes, including the precise size and setback
requirements.Thus, staf recommends acknowledgement of the Preliminary Plat, with the condition that
those requirements be satisfied, as stated previously on the Summary page.
PLAT DATA: In reviewing, providing comments, and making recommendations and decisions on a
proposed preliminary plat, the Staff Planning Commission and City Council shalluse the following
criteria:
PLAN CHEYENNE.The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in the Plan Cheyenne.
Plan Cheyenne recommends a Future Land Use Category of Urban Residential for this area. The Urban
Residential category allowsfor a broader variety of residential types, including single-family residences,
